<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST494"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 2:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop...I thought it would be obvious, but apparently it wasn&#39;t.  I was joking.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 494-->
<!--Post: 942--><!--Time: 1093724463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST942"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sapper<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sapper<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 28, 2004 - 1:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Her is a possible scinero for the missing years. <BR>I honestly dont think he stopped killing. He just moved his activities else where. So how does theory strike you? <BR>The BTK got a job working for Boeing in the 70&#39;s. <BR>Somewhere in the early 80&#39;s he was transfered to Seattle countinued to kill up there. &#40; he would be just one among many serial killers there&#41;. Then he gets layed off in the post 9-11 years and goes back to Wichita. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 942-->
<!--Post: 1422--><!--Time: 1100886649-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, November 19, 2004 - 9:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I like Sapper&#39;s theory.  I grew up in Wichita, where my dad worked as an engineer for Boeing.  In 1990, he transfered to the Oklahoma City Boeing location because he and the other engineers were informed that, eventually, there would be no more engineering at the Wichita location.  &#40;Which, by the way, did NOT come to pass, although my dad continues to work for Boeing in OKC, as does my husband.&#41;  All of the Boeing Wichita engineers began looking to transfer to Seattle, Huntsville, Alabama, etc.  Perhaps BTK was/is a Boeing engineer, and was transfered elsewhere at about the same time as my dad.  Like I said, engineering never really left Wichita after all, and I know of several Boeing engineers who have returned to the area, or travel there periodically from other Boeing locations.  My dad and husband are just two Boeing engineers who travel there regularly.  &#40;No, neither one of them is BTK!&#41;  Another BTW, Wichita is only two hours north of Oklahoma City, an easy, straight shot up I-35.  Hey, BTK, you work for Boeing?  Maybe in OKC?       <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1422-->
<!--Post: 2526--><!--Time: 1103758482-->
