<!--Post: 2627--><!--Time: 1103855959-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2627"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 6:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looking back over the posts in this thread the Wichita-Seattle link first posed by Sapper is most interesting. I am not sure when Boeing and McDonnell merged. In the time frame 1974--1990 say what other locations did Boeing have where personnel might get transferred?  We need the help of a Boeing person from Wichita who would know this or could find it out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2627-->
<!--Post: 2628--><!--Time: 1103856838-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2628"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 6:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That Seattle theory would also be plausible in reverse.  Perhaps he worked in Seattle, but traveled to Wichita for training periodically,  That would account for the time frame&#40;s&#41; between murders; &#34;traveling businessman&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2628-->
<!--Post: 2680--><!--Time: 1103914238-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2680"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 10:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the traveling businessman idea is plausable however it seems that btk has knowledge of the area how many business men have time to stalk victims on a business trip. &#40;they often don&#39;t allow for that type of dedicated use of non company time&#41; <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2680-->
<!--Post: 2683--><!--Time: 1103920653-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2683"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I travel for business often and nights in hotels rooms get extremely boring.  There is plenty of time to read maps, take walks, etc. I don&#39;t know the Wichita area, but are/were there any hotels near the crime scenes?  Would explain the quick getaway and clean up.  The room&#40;s&#41; would be cleaned daily, thus no evidence and no one would think to search a hotel.  Just going with the theory...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2683-->
<!--Post: 2761--><!--Time: 1104084039-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2761"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oklahoma Mike:  See my 11/19 post regarding Boeing Wichita transfers.  My family has a long time association with Boeing.  Seattle, Huntsville, and OKC are just three places where Wichita Boeing personnel transferred  &#40;BTW, my dad worked with Vicki Wegerle at Boeing before she left to stay home with her children.&#41; <BR>Dee:  There is indeed a hotel near quite near some of the crime scenes that Boeing uses  ALL THE TIME, and has used for years, to house Boeing employees visiting Boeing/Wichita.  My dad has stayed there many time in the past, and my husband stays there nearly every time he travels to Boeing in Wichita.  The name of it is The Wichita Suites.  Map its location, then compare it to the map of the BTK crime scenes.  Great theory; I like it.   <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2761-->
<!--Post: 3042--><!--Time: 1104379473-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3042"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Ksugirl.  I mapped it out and there is no more than 4 miles from the Suites to the crime scenes; excluding the one on W 13th-which we all know was way out of the &#34;normal&#34; area.  Just a thought...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3042-->
<!--Post: 6977--><!--Time: 1108101443-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 9:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The BTK got a job working for Boeing in the 70&#39;s.  Somewhere in the early 80&#39;s he was transfered to Seattle countinued to kill up there. &#40; he would be just one among many serial killers there&#41;. Then he gets layed off in the post 9-11 years and goes back to Wichita.&#34; <BR>------- <BR> <BR>Now that you say that... I was reading about the reporter who got the first BTK letter. She never told anybody, not even the police, where or how she got the letter. So, some short time later she moved to Eugene Oregon, then to Seattle. Funny you said that. I wonder if she is still in journalism.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6977-->
